---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { lakeFaqs, lakeSources, lakePlanningReviewedAt } from '../data/lakePlanning';
const topics={science:'Colour and science',ice:'Ice and skating',water:'Water activities',journey:'Choosing and reaching a lake'};
---
<BaseLayout title="Banff Lake FAQ — Blue Water, Ice, Swimming & Canoes" description="Why are Banff lakes blue? What does frozen-looking ice mean? Find sourced answers about swimming, canoes, Moraine access and choosing a lake day." lastUpdated={lakePlanningReviewedAt}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({ '@context':'https://schema.org', '@type':'FAQPage', mainEntity:lakeFaqs.map(faq=>({ '@type':'Question',name:faq.question,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:faq.answer} })) })} />
  <div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Lakes',href:'/lakes'},{label:'Lake FAQ and Science'}]} /></div>
  <section class="page-hero"><img src="https://banfflakelouise.bynder.com/m/1e85056f0193bfe9/1500x915_jpg-2022_LakeLouise_Friends_ROAMCreative.jpg" alt="A canoe outing at Lake Louise" class="page-hero-bg" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" /><div class="page-hero-content"><span class="badge">Look a Little Closer</span><h1>Banff Lakes: Questions &amp; Science</h1><p>Understand the colour, separate appearance from conditions, and choose what to check for your actual lake day.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container faq-page">
    <div class="science-panel"><h2>How rock becomes part of the view</h2><p>Moving glacier ice grinds bedrock into sediment. The finest material, called rock flour, can remain suspended in meltwater. Light interacting with those particles helps create the cloudy blue, green and milky appearance associated with many glacier-fed lakes.</p><ol class="science-flow"><li><span aria-hidden="true">🏔️</span><strong>Glacier and bedrock</strong><p>Grinding produces particles ranging from large fragments to very fine sediment.</p></li><li><span aria-hidden="true">〰️</span><strong>Meltwater transport</strong><p>Fine material can travel in streams and remain suspended in lake water.</p></li><li><span aria-hidden="true">☀️</span><strong>Sediment and light</strong><p>Scattering changes how the water appears to an observer.</p></li></ol><p>This is an explanation of a physical process, not a colour forecast or a claim that one Banff lake has the most sediment. A photograph does not establish what your own visit will look like.</p><p><a href={lakeSources.flour} target="_blank" rel="noopener">National Park Service: glacial flour ↗</a> · <a href={lakeSources.colour} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Glacier National Park: the turquoise mechanism ↗</a></p></div>
    <div class="quick-grid"><article><h2>For a winter lake visit</h2><p>Plan the designated land approach or a currently operating managed rink. This guide has no ice sensor or current water-temperature reading. A cold forecast, a month name or another person's tracks cannot establish conditions along a route.</p><p><a href="/activities/ice-skating">Choose a rink and check its status</a> · <a href="/winter">Compare other winter days</a></p></article><article><h2>For a water activity</h2><p>Start with permission at the exact waterbody, then equipment, experience, weather and recovery arrangements. Cold immersion can impair breathing and movement rapidly; closeness to shore and swimming ability do not remove that risk. Wear a properly fitted, approved flotation device for the activity.</p><p><a href={lakeSources.flotation} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Transport Canada: flotation and cold water ↗</a> · <a href="/paddling">Lake and river planning</a></p></article></div>
    <h2 id="questions">Find your question</h2><form class="faq-filters" id="faq-filters" aria-label="Filter lake questions" hidden><div><label for="lake-question-search">Search questions and answers</label><input type="search" id="lake-question-search" placeholder="Ice, canoes, Peyto, colour…" /></div><div><label for="lake-question-topic">Topic</label><select id="lake-question-topic"><option value="all">All topics</option>{Object.entries(topics).map(([value,label])=><option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></div><button type="button" class="btn btn-outline" id="faq-reset">Reset question filters</button></form><p id="faq-count" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">{lakeFaqs.length} questions</p><noscript><p>All questions and answers are available below without JavaScript.</p></noscript><p id="faq-empty" class="notice" hidden>No question matches. Clear the search or choose another topic. The <a href="/lakes">lake comparison</a> and <a href="/paddling">paddling guide</a> offer more planning detail.</p>
    <div class="faq-list">{lakeFaqs.map(faq=><details id={'question-'+faq.id} data-topic={faq.topic} data-question-search={(faq.question+' '+faq.answer).toLowerCase()}><summary>{faq.question}</summary><div class="answer"><p data-answer>{faq.answer}</p><a href={faq.source} target={faq.source.startsWith('https:')?'_blank':undefined} rel={faq.source.startsWith('https:')?'noopener':undefined}>{faq.label} {faq.source.startsWith('https:')?'↗':'→'}</a></div></details>)}</div>
    <div class="next-plan"><h2>Turn the answer into a day</h2><p>Choose the main experience, then check its actual journey and return. A lake view does not need to become a full hike or a paddle to be worthwhile.</p><a href="/lakes#lake-plans" class="btn btn-primary">Compare 10 lake plans →</a><div class="next-links"><a href="/accessible-trails">Physical access features</a><a href="/parking">Parking and arrival</a><a href="/shuttle-reservations">Reserved lake journeys</a><a href="/packing-list">Packing checklist</a><a href="/conditions">Official conditions sources</a></div></div><p class="small">Reviewed October 29, 2026. Linked sources establish the stated science, rules and planning information; they do not establish today's opening, ice thickness, water temperature, rental availability or individual suitability.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  const form=document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#faq-filters');
  const search=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#lake-question-search');
  const topic=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#lake-question-topic');
  const count=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#faq-count');
  const empty=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#faq-empty');
  const items=Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDetailsElement>('[data-question-search]'));
  if(form&&search&&topic&&count&&empty) {
    const update=()=>{
      const query=search.value.trim().toLowerCase();let found=0;
      items.forEach(item=>{const match=(!query||item.dataset.questionSearch?.includes(query))&&(topic.value==='all'||item.dataset.topic===topic.value);item.hidden=!match;if(match)found++;});
      count.textContent=found+' of '+items.length+' questions';empty.hidden=found!==0;
    };
    search.addEventListener('input',update);topic.addEventListener('change',update);
    form.addEventListener('submit',event=>event.preventDefault());
    document.querySelector('#faq-reset')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{form.reset();update();});
    form.hidden=false;update();
  }
</script>
<style>
  [hidden]{display:none!important}.faq-page{max-width:1100px}.faq-page p{line-height:1.75;margin:.7rem 0 1rem}.faq-page h2{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;scroll-margin-top:6rem}.science-panel{background:var(--color-primary);color:var(--color-white);padding:2rem;border-radius:var(--radius)}.science-panel h2{color:var(--color-white);margin-top:0}.science-panel a{color:#f4d4a8;text-decoration:underline}.science-flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));list-style:none;padding:0;gap:1.2rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.science-flow li{padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid #93a897;border-radius:8px}.science-flow strong,.science-flow span{display:block}.science-flow span{font-size:2rem;margin-bottom:.5rem}.science-flow p{font-size:.9rem}.quick-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.25rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.quick-grid article,.next-plan{padding:1.5rem;background:var(--color-bg-alt);border-radius:var(--radius)}.quick-grid h2,.next-plan h2{margin-top:0;font-size:1.6rem}.faq-filters{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:end;padding:1.25rem;background:var(--color-bg-alt);border-radius:8px}.faq-filters>div{display:flex;flex:1 1 230px;flex-direction:column;gap:.4rem}label{font-weight:700}input,select{font:inherit;color:inherit;padding:.7rem;background:white;border:1px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;width:100%}.faq-list details{border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:.5rem 0}.faq-list summary{font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;padding:.8rem 0}.answer{padding:0 1rem 1rem}.answer a{font-size:.88rem}.notice{padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:8px}.next-plan{margin:2rem 0}.next-links{display:flex;gap:.7rem 1.2rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1rem}.small{font-size:.83rem;color:var(--color-text-light)}a:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.science-flow,.quick-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.science-panel{padding:1.25rem}.faq-filters>div{flex-basis:100%}.answer{padding-left:.25rem}.btn{white-space:normal}}
</style>
